# Response headers for the Tetris Lab (ticket 17). Vite copies this file from
# `web/public/` to `dist/_headers`, which is the directory Wrangler reads it from.
# The file itself is never served: Workers Static Assets treats `_headers` and
# `_redirects` as configuration, so `GET /_headers` is the SPA fallback, not this.
#
# The rules apply to static-asset responses only. That is why the Worker has no
# `main` (see `web/wrangler.jsonc`): a script's responses ignore this file.
#
# Shape proven on this account by `host-probe/src/_headers` (ticket 09), live at
# lab.samibentaleb.com. Two rules of the platform decide the layout:
#
#   * `.wasm` is already inferred as `application/wasm` from the extension, so the
#     first rule is a tripwire, not the mechanism;
#   * same-name headers from matching rules are **comma-joined**. So exactly one
#     rule may set `Cache-Control` for a given URL, which is why `/*` below sets
#     only `X-Content-Type-Options`: adding a Cache-Control there would turn
#     `immutable` into `immutable, public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`.
#
# `scripts/verify.sh` asserts the *effects* of this file over the wire, because the
# file itself cannot be read back.

# 1. The wasm module, pinned. `compileStreaming` in the loader requires it.
/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm

# 2. Fingerprinted assets cache forever. The rule is `/assets/*` and not
#    `/assets/engine-*.wasm`, because the directory is the stable thing and the
#    filenames are not: every future Vite asset — the entry chunk, the worker, the
#    css, the source maps — lands under this rule automatically.
#    ETag is a platform default and needs no line here.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# 3. The page always revalidates. These two rules restate the platform default, so
#    a change to that default cannot silently ship a stale shell. `/` is the URL a
#    visitor (and the smoke test) asks for; `/index.html` is matched whatever
#    `html_handling` rewrites it to. One rule each: patterns are exact unless they
#    carry a `*`, so these two never match the same URL and cannot be joined.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# 4. Everything else — `manifest.json`, anything the fallback serves — keeps the
#    default Cache-Control and gets hardening only. No Cache-Control rule here,
#    ever: see the comma-join note above.
#
#    Cross-origin isolation is not needed in v1 (§7: one wasm instance per worker,
#    no SharedArrayBuffer), so COOP/COEP stay commented — inside this rule, because
#    a pattern block with no live header is rejected as an invalid rule. This is the
#    one-line opt-in if a threaded build is ever wanted; the check is
#      curl -sSI <url> | grep -i cross-origin     (empty is the expected answer)
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
#  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
